ined based on documented findings.</p>\", \"specific_methods\": \"<p><strong>A. Requirements and system design</strong></p><ol><li>Review the current book-record and circulation workflow with intended users.</li><li>Define the data fields, user roles, validation rules, and process flow for the system.</li><li>Prepare the initial interface and database design for review.</li></ol><p><strong>B. Development and integration</strong></p><ol><li>Implement the catalog, borrower, circulation, availability, and reporting features.</li><li>Connect the modules and apply access controls, validation, and record-history safeguards.</li><li>Prepare representative records and scenarios for functional testing.</li></ol><p><strong>C. Testing and evaluation</strong></p><ol><li>Run functional tests for common cataloging, borrowing, return, and reporting tasks.</li><li>Observe representative users completing selected workflows and record usability findings.</li><li>Prioritize corrections and document the recommended next iteration.</li></ol>\"}, \"introduction\": \"<p>Accessible and well-organized book records support efficient learning, information access, and daily library or collection operations. A Book Management System can provide a single source of truth for titles, copies, borrower records, and circulation activity. This proposal presents the development of a focused system that supports reliable recordkeeping, faster transaction lookup, and useful management reports.</p>\", \"leader_email\": \"23-78498@g.batstate-u.edu.ph\", \"leader_title\": null, \"project_title\": \"Book Management System\", \"leader_contact\": \"09170000001\", \"project_leader\": \"Neil Carlo Delmo\", \"executive_brief\": \"<p>The Book Management System will provide a centralized web-based workspace for recording books, tracking availability, managing borrowers, and producing dependable circulation reports. The project will organize the core book-management activities into one accessible system that can be improved through user feedback and iterative testing.</p>\", \"research_agenda\": \"Digital Transformation, ICT Innovation, and Smart Governance\", \"approved_by_name\": null, \"expected_outputs\": {\"patent\": [], \"policy\": [{\"unit\": \"\", \"quantity\": null, \"description\": \"One (1) process guide Documented process guide for maintaining book records and circulation transactions.\"}], \"product\": [{\"unit\": \"\", \"quantity\": null, \"description\": \"One (1) system Functional web-based Book Management System prototype with catalog, borrower, circulation, and reporting modules.\"}], \"publication\": [], \"social_impact\": [{\"unit\": \"\", \"quantity\": null, \"description\": \"One (1) assessment Usability and workflow assessment based on representative users and test scenarios.\"}], \"people_service\": [{\"unit\": \"\", \"quantity\": null, \"description\": \"One (1) user guide User guide and orientation material for authorized staff and borrowers.\"}], \"economic_impact\": [], \"place_partnership\": []}, \"proponent_campus\": \"BatStateU The NEU ARASOF-Nasugbu Campus\", \"responsibilities\": [{\"name\": \"Neil Carlo Delmo\", \"duties\": \"<p>Lead the requirements analysis, system design, development, testing, documentation, and preparation of the project outputs.</p>\", \"percentage\": \"100\"}], \"general_objective\": \"<p>To design and develop a web-based Book Management System that improves the organization, circulation, and monitoring of book records.</p>\", \"proponent_college\": \"College of Informatics and Computing Sciences\", \"cooperating_agency\": null, \"methodology_images\": [], \"related_literature\": \"Software engineering literature emphasizes requirements analysis, iterative development, validation, and user-centered evaluation as foundations for reliable information systems. These principles support the proposed Book Management System by guiding the conversion of book-circulation workflows into validated modules and tested user tasks. The project will apply these concepts while tailoring the implementation to the intended book-record environment.\", \"specific_objectives\": [{\"description\": \"Identify the functional and information requirements for cataloging books, managing borrowers, and recording circulation transactions.\"}, {\"description\": \"Design a clear data structure and user workflow for book records, copies, borrowers, borrowing, returns, and availability status.\"}, {\"description\": \"Develop and integrate the core Book Management System modules with role-appropriate access and validation.\"}, {\"description\": \"Test the system functions and usability using representative book and circulation scenarios, then document recommended improvements.\"}], \"literature_citations\": \"[]\", \"proponent_department\": \"\", \"checked_verified_by_name\": null, \"recommending_approval_name\": null, \"specific_method_objectives\": [{\"heading\": \"Requirements and system design\", \"methods\": [{\"description\": \"Review the current book-record and circulation workflow with intended users.\"}, {\"description\": \"Define the data fields, user roles, validation rules, and process flow for the system.\"}, {\"description\": \"Prepare the initial interface and database design for review.\"}]}, {\"heading\": \"Development and integration\", \"methods\": [{\"description\": \"Implement the catalog, borrower, circulation, availability, and reporting features.\"}, {\"description\": \"Connect the modules and apply access controls, validation, and record-history safeguards.\"}, {\"description\": \"Prepare representative records and scenarios for functional testing.\"}]}, {\"heading\": \"Testing and evaluation\", \"methods\": [{\"description\": \"Run functional tests for common cataloging, borrowing, return, and reporting tasks.\"}, {\"description\": \"Observe representative users completing selected workflows and record usability findings.\"}, {\"description\": \"Prioritize corrections and document the recommended next iteration.\"}]}], \"literature_research_history\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"Book Management System improves organization circulation monitoring records Identify functional information requirements cataloging books managing borrowers-1786871429978\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"Book Management System improves organization circulation monitoring records Identify functional information requirements cataloging books managing borrowers\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Book Management System\\\",\\\"context\\\":[\\\"Project title\\\",\\\"General objective\\\",\\\"Specific objectives\\\"],\\\"resultCount\\\":12,\\\"searchedAt\\\":\\\"2026-08-16T09:10:29.979Z\\\"}]\"}', 'proposal-packages/1/c5fe1101-201a-4d74-aae6-be54ac18741f/draft-history/detailed_proposal/b3daa153-e99b-454f-a6af-6a3e8046a3b6.pdf', 'book-management-system-detailed-research-proposal.pdf', 'application/pdf', 261084, '5e91d51a45f6ee5a8e5c5979e24971fd8a4e41bfc50eadd2a731a47a0ca08abe', '2026-08-16 11:00:45', '2026-08-20 01:23:05', '2026-08-20 01:23:05'),
