controlled orchard setting.</p>\", \"proponent_college\": \"College of Engineering\", \"cooperating_agency\": null, \"methodology_images\": [{\"id\": \"4b784063-6ae2-44a6-99b3-150c28419d42\", \"path\": \"proposal-drafts/2/5/detailed-proposal/methodology-images/QipcAPbnM602jthiuJVE5XEuoJ9L3epx35y48Kn6.png\", \"size\": \"medium\", \"caption\": \"sample\", \"section\": \"research_design\", \"alignment\": \"center\", \"mime_type\": \"image/png\", \"original_filename\": \"Screenshot 2026-08-09 201715.png\"}], \"related_literature\": \"Research on precision agriculture shows that low-cost sensing and structured field records can improve crop monitoring. Fruit-drop observations are more useful when they are time-stamped, linked to orchard conditions, and reviewed consistently across a growing period.\\n\\nThis study focused on the design, implementation, and evaluation of an Artificial Intelligence of Things prototype designed to provide real-time and accurate predictions of intravenous fluid drip rates. To achieve this, the researchers utilized a Throw Away Prototyping method to construct the physical hardware, which integrated sensors with a microcontroller. They developed machine learning models using Random Forest and XGBoost algorithms to classify the fluid drip status from the collected sensor data. Additionally, the software development costs were calculated using the Function Point IFPUG method, incorporating the accuracy levels of the trained models. System requirements and the dataset construction formulas were derived from existing literature and online health resources. This integrated approach aims to advance the development of adaptive and practical infusion monitoring systems suitable for clinical healthcare environments.<span data-proposal-citation=\\\"3\\\"> [1]</span>\", \"specific_objectives\": [{\"description\": \"Design a low-cost sensor and image-assisted workflow for recording mangosteen fruit-drop events.\"}, {\"description\": \"Test the prototype for detection accuracy, timing, and usability during scheduled orchard observations.\"}, {\"description\": \"Prepare a practical monitoring guide that growers can use to interpret fruit-drop records.\"}], \"literature_citations\": \"[]\", \"proponent_department\": \"College Research Office\", \"checked_verified_by_name\": null, \"recommending_approval_name\": null, \"specific_method_objectives\": [{\"heading\": \"Prototype development and field validation\", \"methods\": [{\"description\": \"Configure the sensor and image-assisted observation setup for the selected orchard section.\"}, {\"description\": \"Compare recorded events with manual validation logs during the observation period.\"}]}], \"literature_research_history\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"Mangostene Fruit Drop Detection System evaluate prototype detecting mangosteen events controlled orchard setting low cost sensor-1787724770334\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"Mangostene Fruit Drop Detection System evaluate prototype detecting mangosteen events controlled orchard setting low cost sensor\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mangostene Fruit Drop Detection System\\\",\\\"context\\\":[\\\"Project title\\\",\\\"General objective\\\",\\\"Specific objectives\\\"],\\\"resultCount\\\":0,\\\"searchedAt\\\":\\\"\\\"}]\"}', 'proposal-drafts/2/5/revision/detailed_proposal/friWqNnNbSuYw4Xfe02oZCiSwoUr5Zxq6NtfxSt9.docx', 'mangostene-fruit-drop-detection-system-detailed-research-proposal.docx', 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document', 447237, 'db801003e30bfd4d803ea7a9f0a826400d09bf04b8b85833580d2ef7368a8730', '2026-09-01 23:40:15', '2026-09-01 23:40:15', '2026-09-02 00:08:30'),
(55, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, 'line_item_budget', 0, 7, 0, 'saved', 'Exact downloaded file staged for revision submission.', 'Replaced Attachment B: Line-Item Budget with mangostene-fruit-drop-detection-system-line-item-budget.pdf.', '[{\"after\": \"Updated PDF contents\", \"field\": \"checksum\", \"label\": \"File contents\", \"before\": \"Previous PDF contents\"}]', NULL, '{\"staff\": [], \"amounts\": {\"other_mooe\": null, \"rent_lease\": null, \"contingency\": null, \"ict_equipment\": null, \"office_supplies\": null, \"postage_courier\": null, \"general_services\": null, \"office_equipment\": null, \"travelling_local\": null, \"supplies_materials\": null, \"telephone_expenses\": 3000, \"other_mooe_expenses\": null, \"repairs_maintenance\": null, \"travelling_expenses\": null, \"printing_publication\": null, \"training_scholarship\": null, \"professional_services\": null, \"subscription_expenses\": null, \"communication_expenses\": null, \"other_general_services\": null, \"representation_expenses\": null, \"other_supplies_materials\": null, \"other_machinery_equipment\": null, \"semi_expendable_equipment\": null, \"machinery_equipment_outlay\": null, \"other_professional_services\": null, \"technical_scientific_equipment\": null}, \"certified_by\": null, \"approval_body\": \"lrec\", \"leader_campus\": \"ARASOF-Nasugbu\", \"level_of_call\": \"central_agency\", \"certified_role\": null, \"leader_college\": \"College of Engineering\", \"custom_co_items\": [], \"resolution_year\": null, \"custom_mooe_items\": [], \"resolution_number\": null}', 'proposal-drafts/2/5/revision/line_item_budget/Ko1lW711Bmm9G5NsYPZmEYUvRKdR57f0QzGkRsK6.pdf', 'mangostene-fruit-drop-detection-system-line-item-budget.pdf', 'application/pdf', 172403, '7f77def3b90d137d51a33c687fc66901efacfb0b76a95c27cf6cc67aea9283e8', '2026-09-01 23:41:28', '2026-09-01 23:41:28', '2026-09-02 00:08:36');
