(56, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, 'detailed_proposal', 0, 9, 1, 'saved', 'Exact downloaded file staged for revision submission.', 'Replaced Detailed Research Proposal with mangostene-fruit-drop-detection-system-detailed-research-proposal.docx.', '[{\"after\": \"Updated PDF contents\", \"field\": \"checksum\", \"label\": \"File contents\", \"before\": \"Previous PDF contents\"}]', NULL, '{\"sdgs\": [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\"], \"staff\": null, \"rationale\": \"<p>Unexpected mangosteen fruit drop can reduce harvest quality and make orchard management difficult. Growers need timely, organized information about when and where fruit-drop events occur. A simple detection and monitoring system can support evidence-based decisions while remaining practical for local farms.</p>\", \"references\": \"Food and Agriculture Organization. (2024). Digital tools for smallholder crop monitoring.\\n\\nSantos, M. (2025). Sensor-assisted fruit monitoring in tropical orchards. Journal of Smart Agriculture, 8(2), 44-58.<p>[1] U. N. Surabaya, D. W. Purnama, R. S. Dewi, et al., &quot;Cost Estimation Using Function Point for an AIoT-Based Infusion Drop Detection Prototype Using Random Forest and XGBoost,&quot; International Journal of Multidisciplinary Research and Analysis, vol. 09, no. 01, Everant Journals, 2026. doi: 10.47191/ijmra/v9-i1-37. [Online]. Available: https://doi.org/10.47191/ijmra/v9-i1-37.</p>\", \"methodology\": {\"data_analysis\": \"<p>Detection records will be summarized using descriptive statistics. Prototype detections will be compared with manual observation logs to estimate agreement, missed events, and false alerts.</p>\", \"research_design\": \"<p>The study will use a design-and-test approach. A prototype detection setup will be installed in a selected mangosteen orchard section and compared with scheduled manual observations.</p>\", \"specific_methods\": \"<p><strong>A. Prototype development and field validation</strong></p><ol><li>Configure the sensor and image-assisted observation setup for the selected orchard section.</li><li>Compare recorded events with manual validation logs during the observation period.</li></ol>\"}, \"introduction\": \"<p>Mangosteen is a high-value fruit crop, but fruit drop before harvest can affect both yield and quality. This sample study explores a practical way to document fruit-drop events and turn field observations into usable farm information.</p>\", \"leader_email\": \"23-73453@g.batstate-u.edu.ph\", \"leader_title\": null, \"leader_contact\": \"09171234567\", \"executive_brief\": \"<p>This sample project develops a practical fruit-drop detection system for mangosteen orchards. The system will combine low-cost sensors and image-assisted observation to detect fruit-drop events, record their timing and location, and help growers identify patterns that can improve harvesting and orchard management.</p>\", \"research_agenda\": \"Smart agriculture and food security\", \"approved_by_name\": null, \"expected_outputs\": {\"patent\": [], \"policy\": [], \"product\": [{\"unit\": \"\", \"quantity\": null, \"description\": \"One (1) prototype A working mangosteen fruit-drop detection prototype with field-ready monitoring guidance.\"}], \"publication\": [], \"social_impact\": [], \"people_service\": [], \"economic_impact\": [], \"place_partnership\": []}, \"proponent_campus\": \"BatStateU The NEU ARASOF-Nasugbu Campus\", \"responsibilities\": [{\"name\": \"Djanisse Villaflor\", \"duties\": \"<p>Leads the prototype design, field validation, data analysis, and preparation of the monitoring guide.</p>\", \"percentage\": \"100\"}], \"general_objective\": \"<p>Develop and evaluate a prototype system for detecting mangosteen fruit-drop events in a controlled orchard setting.</p>\", \"proponent_college\": \"College of Engineering\", \"cooperating_agency\": null, \"methodology_images\": [{\"id\": \"4b784063-6ae2-44a6-99b3-150c28419d42\", \"path\": \"proposal-drafts/2/5/detailed-proposal/methodology-images/QipcAPbnM602jthiuJVE5XEuoJ9L3epx35y48Kn6.png\", \"size\": \"medium\", \"caption\": \"sample\", \"section\": \"research_design\", \"alignment\": \"center\", \"mime_type\": \"image/png\", \"original_filename\": \"Screenshot 2026-08-09 201715.png\"}], \"related_literature\": \"Research on precision agriculture shows that low-cost sensing and structured field records can improve crop monitoring. Fruit-drop observations are more useful when they are time-stamped, linked to orchard conditions, and reviewed consistently across a growing period.\\n\\nThis study focused on the design, implementation, and evaluation of an Artificial Intelligence of Things prototype designed to provide real-time and accurate predictions of intravenous fluid drip rates. To achieve this, the researchers utilized a Throw Away Prototyping method to construct the physical hardware, which integrated sensors with a microcontroller. They developed machine learning models using Random Forest and XGBoost algorithms to classify the fluid drip status from the collected sensor data. Additionally, the software development costs were calculated using the Function Point IFPUG method, incorporating the accuracy levels of the trained models. System requirements and the dataset construction formulas were derived from existing literature and online health resources. This integrated approach aims to advance the development of adaptive and practical infusion monitoring systems suitable for clinical healthcare environments.<span data-proposal-citation=\\\"3\\\"> [1]</span>\", \"specific_objectives\": [{\"description\": \"Design a low-cost sensor and image-assisted workflow for recording mangosteen fruit-drop events.\"}, {\"description\": \"Test the prototype for detection accuracy, timing, and usability during scheduled orchard observations.\"}, {\"description\": \"Prepare a practical monitoring guide that growers can use to interpret fruit-drop records.\"}], \"literature_citations\": \"[]\", \"proponent_department\": \"College Research Office\", \"checked_verified_by_name\": null, \"recommending_approval_name\": null, \"specific_method_objectives\": [{\"heading\": \"Prototype development and field validation\", \"methods\": [{\"description\": \"Configure the sensor and image-assisted observation setup for the selected orchard section.\"}, {\"description\": \"Compare recorded events with manual validation logs during the observation period.\"}]}], \"literature_research_history\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"Mangostene Fruit Drop Detection System evaluate prototype detecting mangosteen events controlled orchard setting low cost sensor-1787724770334\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"Mangostene Fruit Drop Detection System evaluate prototype detecting mangosteen events controlled orchard setting low cost sensor\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mangostene Fruit Drop Detection System\\\",\\\"context\\\":[\\\"Project title\\\",\\\"General objective\\\",\\\"Specific objectives\\\"],\\\"resultCount\\\":0,\\\"searchedAt\\\":\\\"\\\"}]\"}', 'proposal-drafts/2/5/revision/detailed_proposal/i9X67ThaSZuZsea5HCXG607DWr1CvtASmozYBNx2.docx', 'mangostene-fruit-drop-detection-system-detailed-research-proposal.docx', 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document', 447237, 'ee02a150ae48af4b8c83c241b891551c5ca3f9f4853988f0e3592932023f6aa4', '2026-09-02 00:08:30', '2026-09-02 00:08:30', '2026-09-02 00:08:30'),
