849321414, \"id\": \"section-cv-1-awards\", \"label\": \"CV 1 · R&D Awards\", \"width\": 0.8799836588840858, \"height\": 0.09155984210152912, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.059967321508071, \"y\": 0.7955128270336705, \"id\": \"section-cv-1-projects\", \"label\": \"CV 1 · R&D Projects Headed/Conducted\", \"width\": 0.8799836588840858, \"height\": 0.09953226594843416, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.059967321508071, \"y\": 0.13119656815488115, \"id\": \"section-cv-1-publications\", \"label\": \"CV 1 · R&D Related Publications (last 3 years)\", \"width\": 0.8799836588840858, \"height\": 0.13183763292100695, \"pageNumber\": 2}, {\"x\": 0.059967321508071, \"y\": 0.2630342010758881, \"id\": \"section-cv-1-presentations\", \"label\": \"CV 1 · R&D Presentation (last 3 years)\", \"width\": 0.8799836588840858, \"height\": 0.06865619105151581, \"pageNumber\": 2}], \"version\": 1, \"checksum\": \"0c7ffa4c89915b206707e9050b07300e48361720e09e4347f555d33012dd02f0\"}}', 0, 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-13 02:30:05', '2026-09-13 02:30:05'),
(80, 12, NULL, 'detailed_proposal', 0, 'proposal-packages/lifecycle-demo/11/v1/detailed_proposal-0.pdf', 'solar-powered-smart-irrigation-system-for-smallholder-vegetable-farms-detailed-research-proposal.pdf', 'application/pdf', 247707, '6b184542b360283515c3dc8401f4b4444f492cd3a2b1b4512e81c4cc90429f6f', '{\"sdgs\": [2, 6, 9], \"staff\": [], \"rationale\": \"Current practice in sustainable agriculture technology still depends on manual processes and fragmented records. This leads to slow turnaround, limited visibility, and inconsistent reporting. A structured and technology-enabled approach can shorten processing time, strengthen traceability, and make outcomes easier to measure while keeping stakeholders in control of decisions.\", \"references\": \"Mendoza, R. (2024). Photovoltaic irrigation for tropical smallholders. Journal of Agricultural Engineering, 55(2), 33-48. Santos, M. (2025). Applied research methods for community-centered technology. Philippine Journal of Science, 154(2), 101-115.\", \"methodology\": {\"data_analysis\": \"Quantitative results will be summarized using descriptive statistics, while qualitative feedback will undergo thematic analysis.\", \"research_design\": \"The study will use a developmental research design with mixed-method evaluation.\", \"specific_methods\": \"Researchers will review existing workflows, co-design the solution with stakeholders, implement it iteratively, and evaluate it through controlled pilot testing.\"}, \"introduction\": \"The project Solar-Powered Smart Irrigation System for Smallholder Vegetable Farms responds to persistent gaps in sustainable agriculture technology, where fragmented processes limit reliability and responsiveness. This study designs and evaluates a practical solution grounded in the day-to-day needs of its intended users.\", \"leader_email\": \"23-78498@g.batstate-u.edu.ph\", \"leader_title\": \"Mr.\", \"project_title\": \"Solar-Powered Smart Irrigation System for Smallholder Vegetable Farms\", \"leader_contact\": \"09170000004\", \"project_leader\": \"Neil Carlo Delmo\", \"executive_brief\": \"This project will design, build, and evaluate a solar-powered irrigation controller with soil moisture sensing to improve how sustainable agriculture technology is carried out in partner communities and campus units.\", \"research_agenda\": \"Agriculture, Food Security, and Climate Resilience\", \"approved_by_name\": \"Dr. Patricia Anne Villanueva\", \"expected_outputs\": {\"patent\": [], \"policy\": [{\"description\": \"An adoption guide for university and community stakeholders\"}], \"product\": [{\"description\": \"A solar-powered irrigation controller with soil moisture sensing\"}], \"publication\": [{\"description\": \"One peer-reviewed research article\"}], \"social_impact\": [{\"description\": \"Improved access to timely and reliable services for the target community\"}], \"people_service\": [{\"description\": \"A validated usability and acceptance report from pilot participants\"}], \"economic_impact\": [{\"description\": \"More efficient use of institutional and community resources\"}], \"place_partnership\": [{\"description\": \"A working partnership between the university and participating community sites\"}]}, \"proponent_campus\": \"ARASOF-Nasugbu Campus\", \"responsibilities\": [{\"name\": \"Neil Carlo Delmo\", \"duties\": \"Leads project planning, implementation, quality assurance, data analysis, and reporting.\", \"percentage\": 100}], \"general_objective\": \"Develop and evaluate a solar-powered irrigation controller with soil moisture sensing.\", \"proponent_college\": \"College of Accountancy, Business, Economics and International Hospitality Management\", \"_revision_sections\": {\"regions\": [{\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.11314105172442576, \"id\": \"section-project-information\", \"label\": \"I. Research Project Title\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.028846153846153848, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.1419872055705796, \"id\": \"section-research-agenda\", \"label\": \"II. Research Agenda\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.02425208458533654, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.16623929015591613, \"id\": \"section-sdgs\", \"label\": \"III. Sustainable Development Goal\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.16837610750116855, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.33461539765708465, \"id\": \"section-project-team\", \"label\": \"IV. Project Leader and Staff\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.09391021728515624, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.4285256149422409, \"id\": \"section-proponent\", \"label\": \"V. Proponent Agency\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.0623931884765625, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.4909188034188034, \"id\": \"section-cooperating-agency\", \"label\": \"VI. Cooperating Agency\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.023183773725460734, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.5141025771442641, \"id\": \"section-executive-brief\", \"label\": \"VII. Executive Brief\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.04946579892411191, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.5635683760683761, \"id\": \"section-rationale\", \"label\": \"VIII. Rationale\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.07767095321264023, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.6412393292810163, \"id\": \"section-objectives\", \"label\": \"IX. Objectives of the Project\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.15085468129215077, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.7920940105731671, \"id\": \"section-expected-outputs\", \"label\": \"X. Expected Output of the Project\", \"width\": 0.8518791261062123, \"height\": 0.1278846202752529, \"pageNumber\": 1}, {\"x\": 0.07401960659650417, \"y\": 0.91997863084842, \"id\": \"section-literature\", \"label\"